  ('Physics', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2', 'Motion and Forces', 'What is inertial mass?', 'A measure of how difficult it is to change an object''s velocity: m = F/a.', 18),
  ('Physics', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2', 'Motion and Forces', 'What is weight?', 'The force acting on an object due to gravity: W = mg.', 19),
  ('Physics', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2', 'Motion and Forces', 'What is the difference between mass and weight?', 'Mass is the amount of matter (kg) and doesn''t change; weight is a force (N) that depends on gravity.', 20),
  ('Physics', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2', 'Motion and Forces', 'What is momentum?', 'Mass × velocity: p = mv, measured in kg m/s.', 21),
  ('Physics', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2', 'Motion and Forces', 'What is the law of conservation of momentum?', 'In a closed system, the total momentum before an event equals the total momentum after.', 22),
  ('Physics', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2', 'Motion and Forces', 'What is the equation linking force and change in momentum?', 'F = (mv − mu) ÷ t.', 23),
  ('Physics', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2', 'Motion and Forces', 'Why do seat belts and airbags reduce injuries?', 'They increase the time taken for the person to stop, reducing the rate of change of momentum and so the force.', 24),
  ('Physics', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2', 'Motion and Forces', 'What is stopping distance?', 'Thinking distance + braking distance.', 25),
